.TH EUCLID-CLI-ESM-START-BUCKET 1 "October 2026" "euclid-cli 1.0.53" "Euclid CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
euclid-cli-esm-start-bucket \- deliver a stopped bucket's held events
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B euclid-cli esm start-bucket
.BR \-\-bucket | \-b
.I NAME|ERN
.SH DESCRIPTION
Starts a bucket stopped with
.BR euclid-cli-esm-stop-bucket (1).
Every event held for it becomes deliverable again, oldest first, with a
fresh retention period, and new events are delivered as they are made.
.PP
Safe to run on a bucket that is not stopped, which releases nothing.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-b ", " \-\-bucket " " \fINAME|ERN\fR
The bucket. Required.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The bucket is started. The answer says how many events were released.
.TP
.B 1
No such bucket, not permitted, or the server failed.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR euclid-cli-esm-stop-bucket (1),
.BR euclid-cli-esm (1)
